\begin_layout Chapter
omg
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Sarsa-200
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Although it is the same benchmark, the results are hardly comparable to
 the Sarsa-75 version.
 Not only is a new performance achieved, but there are no more outlier runs.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Scratch GP Results (MSE 200)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The regular GP runs could completely solve the problem from complexity 18,
 where both the regression error and the average reward were exceptionally
 good.
 Very different results are noticeable in the medium-complex candidates.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The formulas are hardly comprehensible.
 Instead of a distinction between Action 0 and Action 1, a mathematical
 formula is found.
 Potentizing was often done with very high values, often with very high
 values, which was not significant in any humanly considered approach.
 The simplest agents unfortunately show a poor performance in the real evaluatio
n which could not exceed the maximum-momentum solution.
 
\end_layout

